  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "Fixes\n\nEvents whose delegate returns dynamic and takes a ref dynamic (#308, closes #307). An event such as delegate dynamic DynHandler(dynamic x, ref dynamic y) failed to compile (CS0019, CS8716). It now compiles.\n\nPerformance\n\nImposters of members with dynamic types no longer use the runtime binder (#308, closes #307). An imposter kept dynamic arguments, results and values as dynamic, so its own calls with them were dynamic call sites, bound by Microsoft.CSharp's runtime binder on first use. That covered matching a setup and formatting a verification message. It now keeps them as object, and those calls bind when the imposter compiles. What you write against keeps dynamic: Arg\\<dynamic> in setups and Raised, and the Returns, Callback, Throws and indexer delegates.",
